rtÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙøHis prayer also, and how God was intreated of him, and all his sins, and his trespass, and the places wherein he built high places, and set up groves and graven images, before he was humbled: behold, they are written among the sayings of the seers.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpSo Manasseh slept with his fathers, and they buried him in his own house: and Amon his son reigned in his stead.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter!«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]Amon was two and twenty years old when he began to reign, and reigned two years in Jerusalem.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¸But he did that which was evil in the sight of the LORD, as did Manasseh his father: for Amon sacrificed unto all the carved images which Manasseh his father had made, and served them;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwand humbled not himself before the LORD, as Manasseh his father had humbled himself; but Amon trespassed more and more.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFAnd his servants conspired against him, and slew him in his own house.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut the people of the land slew all them that had conspired against king Amon; and the people of the land made Josiah his son king in his stead.¦layout ªlast_verse